# DIAN boundary layer 1 — image-level exclusion (REQ-X3, design §10 Layer 1).
#
# This file ships with the `backend/` Docker build context. The 3-layer
# DIAN boundary per design §10:
#
#   Layer 1 (this file): the Docker build context physically excludes
#     the `parkos_core/dian/cloud/` subtree from BRANCH images. The
#     cloud package never reaches the branch image filesystem, so
#     `import parkos_core.dian.cloud.dispatcher` on a branch container
#     fails at the filesystem layer (ModuleNotFoundError) before the
#     module-level import guard even runs.
#
#   Layer 2 (module-level guard): each cloud-only module checks
#     `os.environ.get("PARKOS_DEPLOY", "cloud").lower() == "branch"`
#     at module load and raises ImportError. Belt-and-suspenders for
#     the case where Layer 1 was misconfigured (e.g., someone moved
#     the source).
#
#   Layer 3 (artifact-level filter): the OpenAPI generation scripts
#     tag-filter the cloud-only endpoints OUT of the branch OpenAPI
#     artifact (`api_sucursal/openapi.json`). See
#     `openspec/scripts/build_openapi_artifacts.py` (T-PR6-13).
#
# The branch Dockerfile (T-PR9-04, infra/docker/Dockerfile.branch)
# copies `backend/` as the build context. The cloud Dockerfile
# (T-PR9-04, infra/docker/Dockerfile.cloud) ALSO uses this .dockerignore
# but explicitly does NOT exclude `**/dian/cloud/**` — wait, actually
# cloud images DO need the dispatcher. So this .dockerignore is
# context-dependent.
#
# Resolution: the per-image .dockerignore override happens at the
# Docker build invocation (the multi-stage Dockerfile's `COPY`
# directives). The branch build explicitly skips the dian/cloud/
# subtree via a dedicated `COPY --exclude` pattern. This top-level
# `.dockerignore` is the FALLBACK safety net if the per-image
# exclusion is forgotten.
#
# Rule: exclude `**/dian/cloud/**` from any build context that
# targets a branch service. The PR9 Dockerfiles respect this.

# Cloud-only DIAN package — excluded from branch builds.
**/dian/cloud/**

# Build artifacts + caches (already in .gitignore but .dockerignore
# is independent).
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
